<title>FRANCE: ITT denies selling Alcatel shares.</title>
<headline>ITT denies selling Alcatel shares.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. group ITT said on Friday there was no truth to Paris stock market talk that it had sold the rest of its shares in Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
<p>&quot;We continue to hold our 4.5 million shares of Alcatel and we do not have the authorisation of Alcatel to sell the remaining stake at this time nor have we sold,&quot; Jim Gallagher, ITT vice-president of public relations, told Reuters.</p>
<p>ITT holds 2.8 percent of Alcatel, or 4.5 million shares, after having sold 2.2 percent on February 13.</p>
<p>Alcatel shares were up 0.68 percent at 591 francs at 1344 GMT after touching an intraday low of 574 francs earlier.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
